  'Building Materials and Construction',
  'Building Materials and Construction introduces the physical, environmental, technical, and professional logic that turns architectural design into built form. Students learn how major materials behave, how assemblies manage structure and enclosure, how details mediate movement and water, how codes and construction sequencing shape decisions, and how carbon, health, labor, safety, cost, and maintenance affect responsible material choices.',
  $bmatjson${"slug": "building-materials-and-construction", "title": "Building Materials and Construction", "description": "Building Materials and Construction introduces the physical, environmental, technical, and professional logic that turns architectural design into built form. Students learn how major materials behave, how assemblies manage structure and enclosure, how details mediate movement and water, how codes and construction sequencing shape decisions, and how carbon, health, labor, safety, cost, and maintenance affect responsible material choices.", "topics": [{"id": "628c4850-114a-46d2-a08f-6d55d6218677", "type": "topic", "title": "Material Thinking and Construction Logic", "description": "This opening section establishes construction as a design discipline. Students learn that buildings are not just represented; they are assembled from materials, labor, systems, tolerances, codes, supply chains, and maintenance realities.", "children": [{"id": "1139cf36-342f-4b7f-9905-8c7666745c4a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "From Design Intent to Built Form", "children": [{"id": "95bcd09f-c7c5-408e-b0ec-ddbdd9750e31", "type": "concept", "title": "Design intent, performance criteria, and detail strategy"}, {"id": "e80fa298-c875-4dba-8231-9b9e272a8d5f", "type": "concept", "title": "Material, assembly, system, and building scales"}, {"id": "d9fe4c0b-9101-4a5f-948c-6d7fa0d1f54d", "type": "concept", "title": "Precedents, standards, and field conditions"}, {"id": "af5b5905-b0b7-4867-be76-e5b25c9a72b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade-offs between expression, cost, performance, and risk"}], "description": "The point is to connect architectural ideas to physical decisions that survive procurement, construction, use, and weather."}, {"id": "bb7ce2cc-3344-4f55-8f2a-66a827b1e929", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assembly Thinking", "children": [{"id": "1c661e0a-cdad-4919-b299-bc0ff38202b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Structure, enclosure, control layers, finishes, and services"}, {"id": "9bcac307-de1d-47f5-bbf5-a1c55877cbe5", "type": "concept", "title": "Load path, drainage path, air path, and thermal path"}, {"id": "dab202c2-4ff6-48b1-bf33-dcde8e4c785a", "type": "concept", "title": "Interfaces and transitions"}, {"id": "902f70c4-5dff-4810-aedc-51654d81236e", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance, repair, and replacement thinking"}], "description": "Students learn to see walls, roofs, floors, and openings as layered systems with jobs to do."}, {"id": "4d431a8c-3e1f-4a74-932f-cab35c7641fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Construction Culture and Responsibility", "children": [{"id": "cd2b34c6-d928-420a-8eed-0b4043d58382", "type": "concept", "title": "Architect, contractor, consultant, fabricator, and trades roles"}, {"id": "f89d1ea4-aee6-40e8-a811-a334fe678fbc", "type": "concept", "title": "Shop drawings, RFIs, submittals, and field review"}, {"id": "716d99c2-896c-44d5-bca7-e12bcb7f913a", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, waste, and environmental responsibility"}, {"id": "9d32e4c8-12c8-40e5-94b7-ca4e840c93d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Respect for craft and construction labor"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces the people, contracts, labor, and ethical responsibilities behind material decisions."}]}, {"id": "68315322-cd24-430a-afb9-1499f3d9de3c", "type": "topic", "title": "Material Properties, Testing, and Selection", "description": "This unit gives students the vocabulary to select materials intelligently. The point is to move beyond appearance into measurable behavior, risks, and life-cycle consequences.", "children": [{"id": "1cef56df-d0a1-4503-a08d-bf93aa0e48a9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Physical and Mechanical Properties", "children": [{"id": "81ab27fb-a3b1-43de-b5af-b0e35322cef5", "type": "concept", "title": "Density, strength, stiffness, ductility, hardness, and creep"}, {"id": "7b47cb28-35a6-4a6f-a16a-8b99994d6521", "type": "concept", "title": "Thermal expansion, conductivity, and dimensional stability"}, {"id": "4e7d9bc9-36cd-4d1d-82ce-4afc44a08460", "type": "concept", "title": "Porosity, absorption, permeability, and capillarity"}, {"id": "819b176c-a0b0-49b7-8658-5b029b77c54a", "type": "concept", "title": "Acoustic, optical, and tactile properties"}], "description": "Students learn properties that determine whether a material can carry load, resist damage, and meet design intent."}, {"id": "d14b353e-754e-41af-bdc6-538da1aff652", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Durability, Fire, Moisture, and Weathering", "children": [{"id": "e876f0f0-fe76-4609-bcbb-6c6928bf8c5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Freeze-thaw, UV exposure, corrosion, decay, and abrasion"}, {"id": "3e1bebb4-9cbb-47f6-b870-0ecb2e644afd", "type": "concept", "title": "Fire resistance, combustibility, and smoke contribution"}, {"id": "263b0678-c96a-4e0e-bc08-84d11a3d6f18", "type": "concept", "title": "Moisture storage, drying potential, and mold risk"}, {"id": "28ae00a9-f4a3-40d5-8953-9d2cd7849489", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance cycles and service life"}], "description": "Materials age, burn, corrode, rot, crack, stain, and fail differently; students learn to anticipate those paths."}, {"id": "9529908c-8c74-4a42-a060-8a9248036101", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Selection Criteria and Testing", "children": [{"id": "1d6fb6b0-9827-4a9d-9fdc-9229922c8997", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards, mockups, certifications, and test reports"}, {"id": "9f67edd7-911b-4825-b91f-742eed5cf6c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, availability, lead time, and local skill"}, {"id": "7f9ee81e-b4cb-4936-8e4b-2143440dc477", "type": "concept", "title": "Embodied carbon, toxicity, and responsible sourcing"}, {"id": "069244ef-b0d0-4e3f-a600-a83feb9bd8d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Fitness for climate, code, occupancy, and use"}], "description": "Students practice comparing materials using evidence rather than preference alone."}]}, {"id": "e630e2b3-7a7c-43bd-a45d-a21cee070668", "type": "topic", "title": "Wood and Timber Construction", "description": "Wood is renewable, workable, expressive, and vulnerable. This section covers wood as structure, envelope, finish, and carbon strategy.", "children": [{"id": "3a78ffb5-241b-4222-9916-efa411023c7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Light Wood Framing", "children": [{"id": "074c30ac-d396-4577-bc5b-683adc44746c", "type": "concept", "title": "Stud spacing, plates, headers, joists, rafters, and trusses"}, {"id": "c2c9e53e-f0f3-4f89-b91f-b05e72d44277", "type": "concept", "title": "Shear walls, diaphragms, and lateral load paths"}, {"id": "ad531589-ffe8-4dbf-8d26-f5122c87680f", "type": "concept", "title": "Openings, hold-downs, and connection logic"}, {"id": "4a8ebca0-fb18-42b2-9543-8539bd8fa25c", "type": "concept", "title": "Fire blocking, acoustic separation, and services"}], "description": "Students learn platform framing as a coordinated system of studs, joists, sheathing, openings, fasteners, and bracing."}, {"id": "b8a89ffe-ec9f-4d74-b628-cbcf62e141de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mass Timber and Engineered Wood", "children": [{"id": "9ed66727-284b-4b78-9a5f-f54f6fe13dd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Glulam, CLT, LVL, PSL, and nail-laminated timber"}, {"id": "b1c344ed-ae18-4bd3-a05a-c4ed4f88a5a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Panelization, CNC fabrication, and erection sequencing"}, {"id": "9bd18f96-a2f2-4ba4-ad33-9d1701760693", "type": "concept", "title": "Connections, vibration, fire, and moisture protection"}, {"id": "7e800bd7-3206-4246-b78b-d48463cce1f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Biogenic carbon, forestry, and sourcing claims"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces contemporary timber systems that expand span, height, precision, and prefabrication."}, {"id": "ff0caa97-8ede-4f37-99a1-3aabaa8dff4c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Moisture, Decay, and Detailing", "children": [{"id": "d3ec60ed-1dbf-4e65-a74b-7449f02e9395", "type": "concept", "title": "Rain screens, drainage, and drying"}, {"id": "8e060504-9d5b-43f5-adfe-44de23998967", "type": "concept", "title": "End grain, capillary breaks, and ground clearance"}, {"id": "28771039-3077-48fb-83c0-1e4846e4af45", "type": "concept", "title": "Preservatives, flashing, and ventilation"}, {"id": "8df0b3a7-9b48-42b7-ac66-9be029300a84", "type": "concept", "title": "Termites, rot, checks, and maintenance"}], "description": "Students learn why wood detailing is often moisture detailing."}]}, {"id": "27e2627a-8ac2-4b49-9c95-90f5dda74099", "type": "topic", "title": "Steel and Metals", "description": "This unit covers metals as structural frames, cladding, roofing, fasteners, finishes, and precision components. Students learn how metal performance depends on alloy, shape, connection, protection, and fabrication.", "children": [{"id": "eb56464a-f40c-414d-95e5-a00d07ebf0df", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Structural Steel and Connections", "children": [{"id": "40808408-8ff6-4d0a-aaed-419e900b5ffa", "type": "concept", "title": "Rolled shapes, plates, tubes, joists, and metal deck"}, {"id": "9ec9a2ad-a3c3-45fd-a9a7-a3d8a48e2e41", "type": "concept", "title": "Bolted and welded connections"}, {"id": "2c7bb7c3-a51c-4638-ae7a-62d40276c231", "type": "concept", "title": "Fireproofing, corrosion protection, and galvanizing"}, {"id": "23300389-f1d5-4a41-bd86-675402f75a66", "type": "concept", "title": "Shop fabrication, erection, tolerances, and sequencing"}], "description": "Students study the logic of beams, columns, bracing, decking, bolts, welds, and load transfer."}, {"id": "274fd88b-810a-4b9c-b432-c5b9f341784d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Metal Enclosure and Finish Systems", "children": [{"id": "f1172c0c-16e6-44de-b23d-d28ea97f0ec2", "type": "concept", "title": "Aluminum, stainless steel, copper, zinc, weathering steel, and titanium"}, {"id": "2fc3e845-4518-406c-bf91-b450979a3156", "type": "concept", "title": "Standing seam roofing and metal wall panels"}, {"id": "d8e8ad7f-e546-42b3-9589-e648e3cee610", "type": "concept", "title": "Perforated, expanded, and corrugated systems"}, {"id": "99163b5e-4053-4a83-a3b1-fa027df535d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Patina, staining, galvanic action, and finish durability"}], "description": "Metals can be skins, screens, roofs, ceilings, stairs, rails, and precise finish assemblies."}, {"id": "886083f4-3b31-48ac-9301-a11cf7e74cc7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Metals, Carbon, and Circularity", "children": [{"id": "c2eb7b15-521f-409d-8b94-bf657dbf1eea", "type": "concept", "title": "Embodied carbon and recycled content"}, {"id": "f5254c62-d527-4b6c-b423-56ae1abe9651", "type": "concept", "title": "Disassembly, reuse, and scrap streams"}, {"id": "8d235de4-b271-4c08-a3cf-335d3e58fefd", "type": "concept", "title": "Coatings, toxicity, and maintenance"}, {"id": "e48e104a-724a-42c7-8479-e5d0280d899e", "type": "concept", "title": "Specification choices and supply chain transparency"}], "description": "Students evaluate the environmental profile of metals beyond simple recyclability claims."}]}, {"id": "86e6b921-2996-4758-b06f-d75940da8337", "type": "topic", "title": "Concrete and Cementitious Systems", "description": "Concrete is structural, plastic, massive, durable, carbon-intensive, and deeply tied to formwork and sequencing. Students learn concrete as chemistry, construction process, and architectural material.", "children": [{"id": "64ed61f0-60ae-4232-ac68-6a1d5605cec5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ingredients, Mixes, and Behavior", "children": [{"id": "74a3e2f9-ef16-4f82-81a2-bd64b5b50870", "type": "concept", "title": "Cement, aggregates, water, admixtures, and supplementary cementitious materials"}, {"id": "b849eae8-091c-4650-a3cc-086b4add4bf7", "type": "concept", "title": "Water-cement ratio, curing, shrinkage, and cracking"}, {"id": "bfecee78-7604-4a58-8ad1-714d385abb3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Compressive strength, reinforcement, and cover"}, {"id": "f763595e-a36b-432d-850a-c6456d6de2df", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-carbon mixes and performance specifications"}], "description": "Students learn what concrete is and why mix design affects strength, workability, durability, finish, and carbon."}, {"id": "c5b9f346-03b4-4611-af10-4e427b66c473", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Formwork, Reinforcement, and Placement", "children": [{"id": "1bf02138-005d-451f-8f5b-ad3da2a0b3c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Cast-in-place, precast, tilt-up, and shotcrete"}, {"id": "05b3e030-48f8-44e3-a8d5-61a8a5c670c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Form ties, reveals, joints, and surface finish"}, {"id": "7d4992c8-c306-4b2e-af12-0c22c50880dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Rebar, mesh, post-tensioning, and embeds"}, {"id": "7126ee6d-58ff-414a-8eb2-a8c4e9fb5d51", "type": "concept", "title": "Placement, vibration, curing, and inspection"}], "description": "Concrete architecture is shaped by temporary work, placement procedures, and coordination."}, {"id": "7c1b2aec-5de5-4634-a4f6-6c9854b6ff52", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Durability, Repair, and Expression", "children": [{"id": "5f624000-9ae9-41d6-8048-f5e09ed0c40f", "type": "concept", "title": "Freeze-thaw, chloride attack, carbonation, and corrosion"}, {"id": "da1a2633-4dd1-4b4a-8228-8033aff2ee52", "type": "concept", "title": "Control joints, expansion joints, and movement"}, {"id": "6d9d2b21-817b-482f-b935-1a9c161b7021", "type": "concept", "title": "Architectural concrete, board form, polish, and pigments"}, {"id": "fa186c68-2aed-49c3-a107-2165de6658ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Repair, patching, protection, and adaptive reuse"}], "description": "Students learn how concrete ages and how architects can design for longevity."}]}, {"id": "9e25625d-b070-490c-8125-f4ac7ebcddd5", "type": "topic", "title": "Masonry and Unit Construction", "description": "Masonry teaches modular thinking, craft, compression, water management, and material memory. This section covers unit systems from brick and block to stone and veneer.", "children": [{"id": "648dd1a2-a9e3-497f-9b56-83f1d0bfe22d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Brick, Block, Stone, and Mortar", "children": [{"id": "71994edb-a83a-4cc8-bead-504c2994e9a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Clay brick, CMU, stone, terra cotta, and manufactured units"}, {"id": "1638ac2d-1955-4438-b3fd-12ff86990f21", "type": "concept", "title": "Mortar types, grout, reinforcement, and ties"}, {"id": "abe85229-e4f4-4b09-84b8-b1e34a44d5db", "type": "concept", "title": "Bond patterns, coursing, dimensions, and tolerances"}, {"id": "09e825ee-61b3-4bf5-974e-5a2f548d4a6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Compression, lateral support, and veneer behavior"}], "description": "Students learn the basic components and behavioral logic of masonry systems."}, {"id": "fe720c5a-f79a-4f54-9daa-fd3d1c9aa37a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cavity Walls and Water Management", "children": [{"id": "d994c7ef-8e6d-426a-b749-60d8f941680e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cavities, drainage mats, weeps, flashing, and vents"}, {"id": "3feb25ba-624a-49ce-b0a1-cb392b885455", "type": "concept", "title": "Shelf angles, lintels, control joints, and expansion joints"}, {"id": "8b26ea4c-9cf3-4d4c-89b6-8ba3daaefcee", "type": "concept", "title": "Air barriers and insulation behind veneer"}, {"id": "bdb56816-5c4b-47f7-88a8-6c367bf308bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Efflorescence, staining, freeze-thaw, and maintenance"}], "description": "Masonry walls must manage rain, air, vapor, and structural movement."}, {"id": "aa57abf1-0a8f-4e1f-a3d8-5e69af049010", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Craft, Heritage, and Contemporary Masonry", "children": [{"id": "fe4b57df-8907-45aa-b91c-52791a60a385", "type": "concept", "title": "Load-bearing traditions and modern veneers"}, {"id": "c68183e4-c649-4939-a11a-42c58ccf6ae4", "type": "concept", "title": "Restoration, repointing, and cleaning"}, {"id": "529f4ca5-cff8-4159-9e0b-5f4346ab0ca4", "type": "concept", "title": "Robotic fabrication and custom units"}, {"id": "b57e10fd-d07a-4071-984a-8dcf1a745967", "type": "concept", "title": "Thermal mass, reuse, and local material identity"}], "description": "Students consider masonry's cultural, technical, and environmental roles."}]}, {"id": "b5232fd3-7c8e-46d4-b84a-c462ae130640", "type": "topic", "title": "Glass, Glazing, and Curtain Walls", "description": "Glass is both technical system and cultural symbol. Students learn its optical, thermal, structural, safety, and assembly consequences.", "children": [{"id": "3578f48b-7f6b-488e-ad7e-198d46ac3ecd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Glass Properties and Glazing Types", "children": [{"id": "d48fa25a-5188-49a2-8181-324c2f28879c", "type": "concept", "title": "Annealed, heat-strengthened, tempered, laminated, and insulated glass"}, {"id": "0e84c24f-2782-4a35-a93a-866a0b5e464c", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-e coatings, frit, tint, and bird-safe treatments"}, {"id": "04c53826-1071-4e4f-9ef1-f1d775ad3a85", "type": "concept", "title": "U-value, SHGC, visible transmittance, and glare"}, {"id": "65907a50-0131-4a51-b321-e809dbb25091", "type": "concept", "title": "Acoustics, safety, and impact criteria"}], "description": "Students compare glass products by strength, safety, energy, daylight, and appearance."}, {"id": "3482ce6c-5e86-4568-a700-e399bd076b92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Curtain Wall and Storefront Systems", "children": [{"id": "a3b30e0d-d68e-489c-81eb-6ba72ebe624c", "type": "concept", "title": "Stick-built, unitized, structural glazing, and point-supported systems"}, {"id": "60e84074-8d72-41bd-8e35-b4f4de865743", "type": "concept", "title": "Mullions, anchors, pressure plates, gaskets, and sealants"}, {"id": "34933e75-c533-4a1b-af6d-8f67d25b44ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Thermal breaks, condensation, and perimeter fire safing"}, {"id": "656959f8-1142-4fdd-909b-9532714a25cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Shop drawings, mockups, and performance testing"}], "description": "This subtopic explains how transparent facades are framed, drained, anchored, and coordinated."}, {"id": "8763cf48-70ca-4a2e-bf8b-3f5de0663248", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Facade Design and Risk", "children": [{"id": "2484a0ae-e7f0-445d-a9d6-a477891366a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Solar gain, overheating, and comfort"}, {"id": "a0c3d47b-0619-4c12-822f-2a1cd2da7b57", "type": "concept", "title": "Water penetration and air leakage"}, {"id": "ade4eee2-4c82-4ad2-bfe3-399d38bcca9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Cleaning, replacement, and access"}, {"id": "7b7d359d-ec92-4513-ba2f-df9a1adc567f", "type": "concept", "title": "Embodied carbon and adaptive shading strategies"}], "description": "Students learn where glass buildings succeed and where they fail."}]}, {"id": "c8e7592d-7092-4a9c-81fd-1bc91f2ca465", "type": "topic", "title": "Building Envelope Science: Heat, Air, and Moisture", "description": "This unit gives students the building science needed to understand envelope performance. The point is practical: prevent leaks, condensation, mold, energy waste, and premature failure.", "children": [{"id": "52f440b6-5977-44d9-8fcb-7c795522a873", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Heat Flow and Thermal Bridging", "children": [{"id": "09917238-0230-4149-bfd7-50834ed04b3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Conduction, convection, radiation, and thermal mass"}, {"id": "05367ffa-e4f4-4afc-b982-c7387ad2f1f5", "type": "concept", "title": "R-value, U-factor, and effective assembly performance"}, {"id": "cb0cd4d6-133e-4b67-8f66-4787f659638d", "type": "concept", "title": "Thermal bridges at slabs, balconies, studs, and frames"}, {"id": "b41dafa7-7a87-4df6-ba1d-af02a5962cb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuous insulation and high-performance enclosure design"}], "description": "Students learn how heat moves through assemblies and why continuity matters."}, {"id": "0bf0a44f-2e79-4410-bc21-78929f1a0045", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Air Leakage and Pressure", "children": [{"id": "500b2232-f55f-4958-bb05-0b973b28b41a", "type": "concept", "title": "Stack effect, wind pressure, and mechanical pressure"}, {"id": "ceb64230-3612-469a-afb1-59f401930833", "type": "concept", "title": "Air barriers, compartmentalization, and leakage testing"}, {"id": "4762aa50-ed8e-4297-b7e4-2f41d2911735", "type": "concept", "title": "Penetrations, transitions, and continuity details"}, {"id": "3c05b979-0d28-4fff-9bf3-238bac3cc77f", "type": "concept", "title": "Blower door logic and commissioning"}], "description": "Air movement carries heat and moisture, so students learn to define and protect air-control layers."}, {"id": "0850c99c-b7a7-4e18-b257-b6c28bbbb060", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Moisture Movement and Drying", "children": [{"id": "d30d0043-fa58-4e00-a3de-9fd12f01c978", "type": "concept", "title": "Bulk water, capillary action, vapor diffusion, and air-transported moisture"}, {"id": "4b63f30f-10bd-43f6-ade9-18906f809ac5", "type": "concept", "title": "Dew point, condensation, and hygrothermal risk"}, {"id": "c9d05980-e714-4c14-b553-87b4476ee23c", "type": "concept", "title": "Drainage planes, vapor control, and drying potential"}, {"id": "8e7535e4-6cda-4cc6-8829-7a2caac30050", "type": "concept", "title": "Climate-specific envelope strategies"}], "description": "Students learn to predict wetting and drying before failures appear in the field."}]}, {"id": "152b9741-6d3a-437b-bf18-f6239ba062e6", "type": "topic", "title": "Roofing, Waterproofing, and Drainage", "description": "Roofs and waterproofing are high-risk assemblies because gravity, wind, UV, foot traffic, and penetrations attack them constantly. Students learn to design for water first.", "children": [{"id": "731d3fbd-f0ea-43a0-ade9-1a8cada60a30", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Low-Slope and Steep-Slope Roofing", "children": [{"id": "4d7637ee-8359-41fb-b842-1cd9e3ca0a56", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-ply, built-up, modified bitumen, metal, tile, slate, and shingles"}, {"id": "4094cfa2-5fd6-4f8e-a2eb-3a76afb69a3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Warm roofs, vented roofs, protected membrane roofs, and green roofs"}, {"id": "ebb7f6eb-1099-49ee-a440-9b2e09eb94e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Parapets, curbs, edges, scuppers, gutters, and downspouts"}, {"id": "3d0c4d35-cbe3-4e05-ab17-0d6fd8ffc971", "type": "concept", "title": "Uplift, fire, hail, and maintenance access"}], "description": "Students compare roof systems by slope, membrane, substrate, insulation, attachment, and maintenance."}, {"id": "e5759810-05fb-4a0c-bbbd-c2076587faa2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Waterproofing and Below-Grade Assemblies", "children": [{"id": "6ce289cf-f059-4aed-946b-e5fbaa1288d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive-side and negative-side waterproofing"}, {"id": "5c04675e-cbf5-49dc-8b5c-ca7b14d9f70e", "type": "concept", "title": "Drainage boards, protection boards, and footing drains"}, {"id": "56e188e8-d2e9-4b11-b41d-a9048b026c36", "type": "concept", "title": "Basements, tunnels, podiums, planters, and plazas"}, {"id": "a300fc91-0b1a-4e97-868a-6d64763fe8fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Hydrostatic pressure, penetrations, and movement joints"}], "description": "This subtopic covers assemblies where failure is expensive and often hidden."}, {"id": "0a87ec24-505c-4c6c-b548-718ecc3fe256", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Drainage Detailing and Failure Prevention", "children": [{"id": "9dc59fe4-6cd3-4846-b736-f46f502b2828", "type": "concept", "title": "Slope, cricket, overflow, and redundancy"}, {"id": "dba16a39-b630-4374-9dcc-ee368b35a44d", "type": "concept", "title": "Flashing, counterflashing, terminations, and sealant limits"}, {"id": "6085370f-a1a1-404e-ba7b-892450e0c099", "type": "concept", "title": "Testing, inspection, and warranties"}, {"id": "2c5c8ed0-0dc7-4a90-95c1-f4762721c9f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Common leak patterns and forensic thinking"}], "description": "Students learn to design details that assume water will arrive and need a path out."}]}, {"id": "ba38fbf3-4123-4e50-b6ef-5a83b4fe7519", "type": "topic", "title": "Foundations, Floors, Walls, Roofs, and Openings", "description": "This section connects primary building assemblies from the ground up. Students learn how each assembly has structural, enclosure, code, service, and finish responsibilities.", "children": [{"id": "1bd53cdd-d81e-451e-bebf-b9bf66d901cb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Foundations and Ground Interfaces", "children": [{"id": "28292a36-e04b-4498-8d32-3c9485bd8e29", "type": "concept", "title": "Shallow footings, slabs, mats, piers, piles, and grade beams"}, {"id": "0d5039bc-7816-46e6-bf1b-33041f5a9240", "type": "concept", "title": "Drainage, capillary breaks, vapor retarders, and insulation"}, {"id": "4c0c875c-b47f-4a6e-9552-7b7c092d9f22", "type": "concept", "title": "Frost depth, bearing, settlement, and waterproofing"}, {"id": "c65feacf-427d-4513-ae59-cc5d31305cec", "type": "concept", "title": "Slab edges, thresholds, and thermal bridges"}], "description": "Students study how buildings meet soil, water, frost, settlement, and radon or vapor risks."}, {"id": "eae05a2a-3163-443b-9677-0a537bef45ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Floors, Walls, and Roofs as Assemblies", "children": [{"id": "ccb6d41a-34a5-481a-97da-52d19de53ce5", "type": "concept", "title": "Substructure, superstructure, enclosure, finish, and services"}, {"id": "8a3550a6-72b8-42ff-8eaf-d9163cddd6e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Span direction, diaphragm action, fire rating, and acoustics"}, {"id": "f1505817-5d7d-4941-9f69-3406147c98f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Roof-wall-floor transitions"}, {"id": "17136fe5-67f7-4d99-ac2c-d7b83a3df9aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Repair access and replaceable layers"}], "description": "This subtopic reinforces layered assembly thinking across the major building parts."}, {"id": "4dc57a75-e935-4723-89a0-b207083e329c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Openings and Penetrations", "children": [{"id": "07063f93-4c6d-4a3a-a596-296d8744889e", "type": "concept", "title": "Rough openings, lintels, sills, jambs, and heads"}, {"id": "9d8c0044-237e-4a25-9818-efee2892f037", "type": "concept", "title": "Flashing, sealants, back dams, and shims"}, {"id": "3c8f4155-f300-41d5-8471-074def408ea8", "type": "concept", "title": "Fire stopping, acoustic seals, and waterproof boots"}, {"id": "84aac871-ef99-4148-9482-e5a1f0c72661", "type": "concept", "title": "Coordination with structure, MEP, and accessibility"}], "description": "Students learn why windows, doors, louvers, vents, and service penetrations are coordination hotspots."}]}, {"id": "5b17bb08-c895-4d2a-a095-ea96453a5e82", "type": "topic", "title": "Insulation, Air Barriers, Vapor Control, and Weatherproofing", "description": "This unit focuses on control layers. Students learn to locate, draw, and preserve insulation, air, vapor, water, and weather-resistive barriers across complete assemblies.", "children": [{"id": "1693b4c1-765e-428a-87da-38b0dc9ae2a1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Insulation Materials and Placement", "children": [{"id": "1f4279a0-6a34-447c-a326-279563bc2039", "type": "concept", "title": "Fiberglass, mineral wool, cellulose, foam, cork, wood fiber, and aerogel"}, {"id": "8cd2b9bf-1c1b-4422-b9e0-9ff88576e69f", "type": "concept", "title": "Cavity, continuous, exterior, interior, and roof insulation"}, {"id": "04c909bd-72d7-4866-aedb-4c4cb01a5eb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Compression, gaps, settling, and installation quality"}, {"id": "7decf59c-dac2-4c11-8a64-fcc2a1e70d71", "type": "concept", "title": "Combustibility, blowing agents, and embodied carbon"}], "description": "Students compare insulation by thermal value, moisture behavior, fire, carbon, installation, and health."}, {"id": "a0aea6bd-e009-4e7e-9911-3e2e78b4a14d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Air and Vapor Control", "children": [{"id": "6dbed7f4-c682-4f67-b1b9-5910863f7a4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Air barrier materials and assemblies"}, {"id": "fae910b4-b722-477b-835d-c916f47beed3", "type": "concept", "title": "Class I, II, and III vapor retarders"}, {"id": "0bed7a96-268c-44c7-a926-6fb6e506ce7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Climate zones and vapor drive"}, {"id": "43194123-7117-4955-977a-cc91eca56e8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Transitions at foundations, roofs, windows, and balconies"}], "description": "This subtopic clarifies the difference between air barriers and vapor retarders."}, {"id": "80074a3f-dc43-409f-ae80-a829c6aea07c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Weatherproofing and Rain Control", "children": [{"id": "cad0e754-8229-4e13-9242-6cb29a16d389", "type": "concept", "title": "Water-resistive barriers and drainage planes"}, {"id": "f6acec60-1732-44be-a56e-b5f92b77c851", "type": "concept", "title": "Rain screens, pressure moderation, and cladding ventilation"}, {"id": "d9e107dd-0291-4d01-8e53-834f29665387", "type": "concept", "title": "Flashing hierarchy and shingle-lap logic"}, {"id": "64c434c3-2022-4880-821b-19efd77dd316", "type": "concept", "title": "Sealants as secondary protection, not primary strategy"}], "description": "Students learn rain-control logic for cladding, openings, and transitions."}]}, {"id": "6a5ef433-6438-499a-90b2-928919cab3ea", "type": "topic", "title": "Detailing, Tolerances, Joints, and Interfaces", "description": "Details are where design intent meets construction reality. This section teaches students to draw and critique details as buildable relationships among materials, movement, tolerances, trades, and performance.", "children": [{"id": "69d991cd-b08c-49a9-b655-c676f9c8d3b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Detail Principles", "children": [{"id": "3562b103-512f-4ad1-8daa-17723b398814", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuity, hierarchy, redundancy, and access"}, {"id": "a3dbf2eb-f477-4dde-906f-bc700bc27fa5", "type": "concept", "title": "Keep water out, let assemblies dry, and avoid trapping moisture"}, {"id": "7942e887-2a43-4ce5-927e-bed6e6de547b", "type": "concept", "title": "Separate incompatible materials"}, {"id": "f275399a-3d16-4af7-98b1-c61b7b8332c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Make construction sequence visible in the detail"}], "description": "Students learn the recurring principles behind good details rather than memorizing isolated examples."}, {"id": "04e3c1a4-5f02-4f6f-9cfd-a1a2cb433e35", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Movement, Joints, and Tolerances", "children": [{"id": "586903a0-5ce2-4ceb-b99f-f34c68aef248", "type": "concept", "title": "Thermal movement, shrinkage, creep, deflection, and settlement"}, {"id": "2557da16-c19d-48d3-a1b2-3ac78baf2155", "type": "concept", "title": "Control joints, expansion joints, isolation joints, and sealant joints"}, {"id": "97e75221-d804-46c5-ad21-773217093f0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Tolerance stacking and field adjustment"}, {"id": "a654f0b3-b933-4147-be91-aae10679870d", "type": "concept", "title": "Differential movement between structure, cladding, and glazing"}], "description": "Buildings move. Students learn to design joints instead of pretending movement will not happen."}, {"id": "a717d24d-6338-467e-8132-29c0ab6d2d1f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interfaces and Constructability", "children": [{"id": "73d09ead-92c6-4d16-b601-fa0fe5261a8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Roof-to-wall, wall-to-foundation, window-to-wall, and balcony-to-wall details"}, {"id": "6bb53491-2ae0-4373-a649-10bdd46b992c", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade sequencing and access for installation"}, {"id": "7f22bf49-2f4b-441a-a5c4-b9506ec01777", "type": "concept", "title": "Fasteners, anchors, embeds, and backing"}, {"id": "efc856c5-3d4c-430e-8226-19bdaceb94bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Reviewing shop drawings and field conditions"}], "description": "This subtopic focuses on the risky edges between systems and trades."}]}, {"id": "c43dfe53-10a3-46c8-a306-f3c772359083", "type": "topic", "title": "Building Systems Coordination and Technical Integration", "description": "Buildings fail when systems are designed in isolation. This unit teaches coordination across structure, enclosure, mechanical, electrical, plumbing, fire protection, accessibility, acoustics, and interiors.", "children": [{"id": "68065654-f2ce-4ad3-9f32-33bcdc255e7b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Structural and Envelope Coordination", "children": [{"id": "f4e5f6b7-92fa-4a37-a45c-9581d06324fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Slab edges, shelf angles, anchors, deflection tracks, and embeds"}, {"id": "39fb90b3-1e40-4ac0-b7e8-df5969ee5f51", "type": "concept", "title": "Lateral drift and facade movement"}, {"id": "e078c91f-8ebc-4a24-b44b-0ec749aac01e", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural penetrations and sleeves"}, {"id": "06eb5c40-4b9b-4961-b634-b5dd994a2407", "type": "concept", "title": "Fireproofing, corrosion protection, and inspection access"}], "description": "Students learn how structure supports enclosure and how enclosure protects structure."}, {"id": "96faa967-7982-44d1-87d1-4e3c246ce73b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MEP, Shafts, and Service Zones", "children": [{"id": "6b1b5547-5282-4d2f-80b6-42ac357e995e", "type": "concept", "title": "Ducts, pipes, conduits, risers, shafts, and ceiling plenums"}, {"id": "754be5d5-fb06-46c1-ba2d-8ca394742eb9", "type": "concept", "title": "Equipment access, maintenance clearances, and roof penetrations"}, {"id": "53765b92-1559-45f2-be50-f3a8b657f656", "type": "concept", "title": "Condensation, acoustics, vibration, and fire stopping"}, {"id": "1b569205-0858-4ba5-ba84-659ac6cf8b5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Coordination drawings and clash detection"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches how services occupy space and affect assemblies."}, {"id": "4aa7904b-971c-4aec-982d-04701310bc4f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interior, Accessibility, and Occupant Performance", "children": [{"id": "7772af84-f298-44af-b246-393c6d4e198e", "type": "concept", "title": "Partitions, doors, stairs, ramps, and guardrails"}, {"id": "d2922473-2044-4c5e-81bf-7b2847e19497", "type": "concept", "title": "Acoustic separation, daylight, IAQ, and thermal comfort"}, {"id": "1c5bab1c-e2fe-4772-a9d7-9ce48efd31bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible clearances and hardware"}, {"id": "68fc7f63-99a0-494f-94cf-f8bdee282819", "type": "concept", "title": "Durability, cleanability, and user maintenance"}], "description": "Students connect construction decisions to human use."}]}, {"id": "a3e09f2a-e900-4cee-8716-75ff012bff36", "type": "topic", "title": "Construction Sequencing, Procurement, and Site Logistics", "description": "This section explains how buildings actually come together over time. Students learn sequencing as a design constraint and a professional communication skill.", "children": [{"id": "8593df09-cf23-42eb-8c8b-0b6a3792fa9f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project Delivery and Procurement", "children": [{"id": "5ca4464d-65e4-470f-84f3-c9505601d39e", "type": "concept", "title": "Design-bid-build, design-build, CM at risk, and integrated delivery"}, {"id": "83273074-ff0c-4718-9b00-68bd2e87851d", "type": "concept", "title": "Subcontractor scopes and bid packages"}, {"id": "4378b78a-bf67-4a4a-b63d-969d51f99bca", "type": "concept", "title": "Long-lead items and substitution requests"}, {"id": "822144a1-23a7-4124-8702-8445bee88e83", "type": "concept", "title": "Submittals, RFIs, change orders, and field directives"}], "description": "Students compare how contract structures affect design control, risk, and collaboration."}, {"id": "5f058c82-2e5e-426a-9fef-b792149fb2e4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Construction Sequence and Logistics", "children": [{"id": "fe60a1b5-e7a5-4feb-8c1f-e53e52cb1a63", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobilization, excavation, foundations, frame, dry-in, rough-in, finishes, commissioning"}, {"id": "759bf174-1f23-40be-a689-70a37ed4bcd6", "type": "concept", "title": "Cranes, hoists, laydown, staging, and site access"}, {"id": "c27eedb7-04a9-4052-acdf-fc5d27317d27", "type": "concept", "title": "Temporary works, shoring, scaffolding, and protection"}, {"id": "dcdb379c-d9a9-4508-983f-0699bd659b99", "type": "concept", "title": "Weather delays and sequencing risk"}], "description": "This subtopic maps the order of operations from site work to handover."}, {"id": "58c1be75-f442-4d4e-9bb4-f8d5e524ebc6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Constructability Review", "children": [{"id": "9e837144-25e4-467e-8327-25a5fd3b9419", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade access, tolerances, and installation paths"}, {"id": "4f190d76-8b8d-4c97-aa53-a07d7cd9ebdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Assembly simplification and prefabrication opportunities"}, {"id": "246d20bc-9ffe-406d-b60b-fd29f40ae71f", "type": "concept", "title": "Field measurement and existing conditions"}, {"id": "4d63c7fd-3a48-4db5-b842-2b77a7ae0ab7", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintainability and replacement planning"}], "description": "Students learn to test a design for buildability before construction exposes the problem."}]}, {"id": "dde57eda-0748-4630-a70f-dd6df1cf4ff8", "type": "topic", "title": "Codes, Fire, Life Safety, Accessibility, and Construction Types", "description": "This unit connects materials and assemblies to legal minimums and public safety. Students learn that code is not a separate topic; it is embedded in every construction decision.", "children": [{"id": "7a564421-1c93-49d2-b648-d4f59e6e4c77", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Construction Type and Fire Resistance", "children": [{"id": "65c70c12-b386-4c8b-aece-dd3215b20c0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Combustible and noncombustible construction"}, {"id": "8fff6af1-bcce-452b-9ced-23ba95424cc5", "type": "concept", "title": "Fire-resistance-rated assemblies"}, {"id": "04769cb1-5c25-4c6f-accf-b22a12c53df8", "type": "concept", "title": "Fire separation, fire stopping, and smoke control"}, {"id": "b6e520cb-32d3-40b6-8227-191d1b85209c", "type": "concept", "title": "Tested assemblies and listed products"}], "description": "Students learn how construction type, occupancy, height, area, and fire ratings shape material choices."}, {"id": "4a08667b-315d-47df-ab64-7f76058b85a8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Egress, Accessibility, and Occupant Safety", "children": [{"id": "154e0b26-4b3e-4ad6-aaf7-aab086bf8a7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Exit access, exits, exit discharge, stairs, doors, and hardware"}, {"id": "0c215b16-ea9d-4791-a127-071581eb7dce", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible routes, clearances, ramps, and thresholds"}, {"id": "9cc8b515-bf42-4a81-945a-0c959c13467f", "type": "concept", "title": "Guards, handrails, slip resistance, and lighting"}, {"id": "2eaaf0aa-3eaa-4b15-9b5f-098eae4aa9f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Signage, alarms, and emergency operations"}], "description": "This subtopic links construction details to safe, equitable use."}, {"id": "bdafd747-d9ef-4e88-b54a-a167c72926cc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Code Documentation and Coordination", "children": [{"id": "6b0b35f3-1cbc-48d9-b2e1-c92504b825ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Occupancy, construction type, and code summary"}, {"id": "8a50a838-9b7f-47a7-ad51-57bfdd4b1f14", "type": "concept", "title": "Rated wall, floor, ceiling, shaft, and door schedules"}, {"id": "28791178-0c9f-4387-87c7-98842466f38a", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility details and mounting heights"}, {"id": "14d98a32-a5f9-47b0-bbd5-470b2b7023fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Inspection, special inspection, and authority review"}], "description": "Students practice translating code obligations into drawings and details."}]}, {"id": "a2282df0-47ae-4d87-8b52-4d8eb8745a7b", "type": "topic", "title": "Sustainability, Embodied Carbon, Life Cycle, and Healthy Materials", "description": "This section makes material responsibility measurable. Students learn to balance performance, carbon, health, durability, reuse, equity, and cost.", "children": [{"id": "2800fcf1-353b-4461-a267-1ded576401a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Embodied Carbon and Life-Cycle Thinking", "children": [{"id": "dd2be884-302b-40d0-a7bd-af60da1fa1e6", "type": "concept", "title": "EPDs, LCAs, product category rules, and carbon accounting"}, {"id": "66f8cf4f-c4f9-4a6c-98a1-d43ce758cda9", "type": "concept", "title": "Structure, enclosure, interiors, and MEP carbon hotspots"}, {"id": "325bf1d6-863a-461b-8baa-7883e586f475", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-carbon concrete, steel reuse, mass timber, and material efficiency"}, {"id": "0379013f-867e-49c1-be47-38c3cccce4e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Operational versus embodied carbon trade-offs"}], "description": "Students learn how material choices affect climate before the building even opens."}, {"id": "d3a31635-73b1-458f-83aa-372c9a260f5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Healthy Materials and Toxicity", "children": [{"id": "8993d9ab-5a01-43ea-8ba0-8023b9b94137", "type": "concept", "title": "VOC emissions, flame retardants, PFAS, PVC, formaldehyde, and red-list chemicals"}, {"id": "5ed71a01-715e-4bb0-a0e0-cb6489492843", "type": "concept", "title": "Indoor air quality and occupant exposure"}, {"id": "9d842d13-4961-4ba9-86fa-226b9d455818", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency labels and certifications"}, {"id": "56c23782-40e2-4530-8e8c-9d8ccb8106b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental justice and extraction impacts"}], "description": "This subtopic evaluates materials through human and ecological health."}, {"id": "730f62df-3e75-4b96-8cb2-066e0912536f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reuse, Circularity, and Adaptive Construction", "children": [{"id": "7211695f-cca8-4a45-8386-aaec091aa711", "type": "concept", "title": "Design for disassembly"}, {"id": "0967dccc-752c-4428-8b89-4a0060663999", "type": "concept", "title": "Salvage, reuse, and material passports"}, {"id": "dc909a9f-5299-4735-9a84-f3be9345d5a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Durability, repairability, and loose-fit strategies"}, {"id": "c47cdd70-e42f-4f4c-9eea-1d6dccd9e82c", "type": "concept", "title": "Waste reduction and construction waste management"}], "description": "Students learn how to design for future change and material recovery."}]}, {"id": "1e454ca7-4da4-419c-aa58-d2ab02d972f2", "type": "topic", "title": "Drawings, Specifications, Mockups, Testing, and Quality Control", "description": "Construction knowledge becomes real through documents, samples, mockups, tests, and field review. Students learn the professional instruments that turn design into verifiable work.", "children": [{"id": "deb45e96-c3df-4392-b346-c4301efaf092", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Construction Drawings and Detail Sets", "children": [{"id": "730b80e6-21a9-4b66-9091-83c2addc0043", "type": "concept", "title": "Plans, sections, elevations, wall sections, and enlarged details"}, {"id": "45a086b5-0e07-4fb8-afed-3cc0d8668be5", "type": "concept", "title": "Dimensions, keynotes, schedules, and references"}, {"id": "583b2901-fc41-4b85-8b4a-f017bd96cf40", "type": "concept", "title": "Coordination with consultant drawings"}, {"id": "647ee19b-7095-40d7-b1bc-1f19d80000c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Drawing hierarchy and revision control"}], "description": "Students learn how drawings communicate scope, geometry, performance, and coordination."}, {"id": "43fe1b15-8ff7-4afe-aec4-12ac52ff0c9e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Specifications and Product Evaluation", "children": [{"id": "6786dee1-106e-4fb7-8fb2-803e6d5b0fdb", "type": "concept", "title": "MasterFormat, section structure, and performance specs"}, {"id": "cb71aee8-1155-4c1b-8015-ecf13842e6de", "type": "concept", "title": "Submittals, samples, substitutions, and alternates"}, {"id": "198a60e4-39ea-42f7-a864-62ca677230bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Manufacturers, warranties, and installation requirements"}, {"id": "99595dd7-a699-48ce-bf5f-ae98e1dc9b2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflicts between drawings and specifications"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces CSI logic and how specs control quality beyond drawings."}, {"id": "fb08b022-1558-4d9f-993b-4851b56831e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mockups, Testing, and Field Quality", "children": [{"id": "8cfe0652-6d56-43d0-a51c-6125e54b3610", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual, performance, and constructability mockups"}, {"id": "a5e5541c-e0d7-4cab-a869-c6bdc4f5f104", "type": "concept", "title": "Air, water, structural, acoustic, and fire testing"}, {"id": "b867ec4d-765f-4778-b6f4-28ceaa309b40", "type": "concept", "title": "Punch lists, inspections, and commissioning"}, {"id": "f46997da-a2c1-4904-810c-7ae2065b65e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Lessons learned and forensic feedback"}], "description": "Students learn why high-risk details need to be tested and observed."}]}, {"id": "bba164c7-6693-4f25-a4c3-9b84dddcd77b", "type": "topic", "title": "Cost, Safety, Labor, Supply Chains, and Constructability Capstone", "description": "The capstone asks students to synthesize material selection, detailing, sequencing, cost, safety, carbon, and labor into a buildable assembly package.", "children": [{"id": "3108b6e4-1142-477b-abbb-6f3de0583fbe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost, Estimating, and Value Decisions", "children": [{"id": "c018df3c-93ff-4b64-8d9f-86d61f723eb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Quantity takeoffs and unit costs"}, {"id": "fe1a4188-cbb1-4014-a9ec-0ca27e8908b3", "type": "concept", "title": "First cost, life-cycle cost, and maintenance cost"}, {"id": "e56ed7cd-588b-48a8-be9f-7ae352c358df", "type": "concept", "title": "Value engineering versus value destruction"}, {"id": "4cb6cfd1-63fd-48c4-b1d4-744ba92f4417", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternates, contingencies, and risk pricing"}], "description": "Students learn that cost is a design variable, not merely a late-stage constraint."}, {"id": "de2b8f35-44c1-455b-99a7-0b8e9c06d650", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Safety, Labor, and Site Ethics", "children": [{"id": "6e37cc37-6e2f-4883-b881-d9d28371344d", "type": "concept", "title": "OSHA basics, fall protection, silica, lifts, and confined spaces"}, {"id": "9f82c8da-3bdf-4b0c-a85f-be7fb6def660", "type": "concept", "title": "Hazardous materials and demolition safety"}, {"id": "84900b58-978d-4d80-b6df-8555d46f6491", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor sequencing, fatigue, and weather exposure"}, {"id": "831ff235-96f4-44d7-8c52-fff4151b3ded", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical design for safe construction and maintenance"}], "description": "This subtopic connects design decisions to worker safety, installation risk, and respect for trades."}, {"id": "2353566c-a873-4028-8584-da0e51147205", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capstone Assembly Package", "children": [{"id": "8b02e7d8-deb5-4d87-bb71-a22d762acb92", "type": "concept", "title": "Material selection matrix"}, {"id": "3dc46dd7-05ab-45c7-bf4c-bec554ed2316", "type": "concept", "title": "Wall section, enlarged details, and control-layer diagram"}, {"id": "04b6cdb0-1b58-44fe-b983-07f55e273a79", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequencing narrative and constructability notes"}, {"id": "3c67411a-858c-495a-b9ce-9ca9604b9f77", "type": "concept", "title": "Carbon, cost, safety, and maintenance reflection"}], "description": "Students produce a coordinated technical package for a selected wall, roof, floor, facade, or interior assembly."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$bmatjson$::jsonb,
  true,
